      "section": "Contact matrix",
      "order": 3,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "A Hi-C matrix drawn as a triangle: x is the position on chr8, y the distance between the two bins, so a TAD reads as a triangle and a loop as a dot at its apex. The collection holds 10, 20 and 40 kb pixels; the tab opens on the 40 kb level for the whole locus, and a zoom (drag on the matrix, or type MYC in the navigator's locus field) re-reads that window at 10 kb. Resolution pins a level, Display flips to the square matrix. Input: the mcool of nf-core/hic, one partition per resolution.\n",
      "wf_tag": "python/advanced_viz_demo"
    },
